/**
 * The world's coastlines, as a bundled asset.
 *
 * Our basemap is a Protomaps archive in R2, and that archive is a deploy
 * artefact — routinely absent in development and on a cold bucket. Without it
 * every map surface in the product used to fall back to a bare drafting
 * graticule: honest, but it read as a wireframe rather than a map. This module
 * is the answer. It carries one generalised outline per country, small enough to
 * ship in a route chunk, so a map can always draw land, water and a border even
 * when no tile ever arrives.
 *
 * **Source.** Natural Earth 1:110m Admin 0 countries, which its authors place in
 * the public domain. Outlines are simplified with Douglas–Peucker at 0.08° and
 * quantised to a hundredth of a degree — roughly a kilometre, which is finer
 * than a country-scale drawing can resolve and far coarser than street level, so
 * callers cap the layer's zoom rather than pretend to a precision it lacks. Only
 * outer rings are kept: lakes and enclaves are not part of a silhouette.
 *
 * **Encoding.** `ISO:ring;ring|ISO:…`, where a ring is a flat list of
 * delta-encoded hundredths of a degree, longitude first. Deltas keep almost
 * every number to two or three characters, which is what makes 8,652 vertices
 * fit in 62KB of source and about 25KB over the wire. Decoding is one pass and
 * memoised, so the cost is paid once per process.
 *
 * **This cut stays as it is.** Two callers need land *synchronously*: the
 * server-rendered world map inlines these paths straight into the document, and
 * the style's ground underlay draws them before any tile can arrive. Neither can
 * await a fetch, and both are sized for this payload. The finer 1:50m cut — the
 * one that knows about the Canaries, Réunion and Guadeloupe — is a separate
 * static asset fetched at runtime by `./countries`, which decodes it with
 * {@link decodeOutlines} below. One encoding, two payloads, one decoder.
 */

/** One closed ring, in degrees, longitude first. */
export type WorldRing = ReadonlyArray<readonly [number, number]>

/** Every outer ring belonging to one country, largest first. */
export type WorldOutline = ReadonlyArray<WorldRing>

/** Hundredths of a degree — the quantisation grid the encoded deltas sit on. */
const SCALE = 100

